<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>Copper Scroll project sites 2026-11-11</name>
<Placemark><name>Tell es-Sultan</name><description>Status: Checked. tell. Position: image, tile F017b (1 Dec 1974) (error approximately 50 m). Ancient Jericho. Mound approximately 270 by 150 m</description><Point><coordinates>35.4443,31.871,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Tulul Abu el-ʿAlayiq, southern mound</name><description>Status: Checked. palace complex. Position: image, tile F017b (error approximately 50 m). Plan test with Netzer 1975 fig. 2; sunken garden wall, pool B107</description><Point><coordinates>35.4367,31.8506,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Birket Musa</name><description>Status: Checked. pool. Position: image, tile F017b (error approximately 50 m). 174 by 143 m on the image; Survey 172 by 144 m</description><Point><coordinates>35.4402,31.8479,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Quruntul, summit enclosure</name><description>Status: Checked. enclosure (modern wall). Position: image, tile F017b (error approximately 80 m). Modern wall with the unfinished church; not the ancient fort (Meshel 1978)</description><Point><coordinates>35.4289,31.8746,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Nebi Musa</name><description>Status: Checked (position and setting). shrine compound. Position: image, tile F017b (error approximately 60 m). Walled compound approximately 65 by 85 m with a court, in a large cemetery; 30 m from the predicted place on the new full-size window; no plan test</description><Point><coordinates>35.4317,31.7867,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Deir Hajla</name><description>Status: Checked. monastery. Position: image, tile F017b (error approximately 50 m). Position, size and layout; compound 40 by 70 m in 1974</description><Point><coordinates>35.5014,31.82,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Khirbet Qumran</name><description>Status: Checked. settlement. Position: image, tile F017b (error approximately 60 m). Plan test with Magen and Peleg 2007 fig. 4</description><Point><coordinates>35.4598,31.741,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>ʿEin Feshkha building</name><description>Status: Checked. building. Position: image, tile F017b (error approximately 60 m). Plan tests with Humbert and Chambon pl. XLIII and Hirschfeld 2004 fig. 3</description><Point><coordinates>35.4525,31.7159,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Hyrcania (Khirbet el-Mird)</name><description>Status: Checked. fort with reservoirs and aqueducts. Position: image, tile F018b; summit of the elevation model 28 m (error approximately 50 m). Reservoirs and fort Checked with plans of Wright and Patrich; aqueduct course mostly not identified</description><Point><coordinates>35.3659,31.7192,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Mar Saba</name><description>Status: Checked. monastery. Position: image, tile F018b (error approximately 50 m). Position only</description><Point><coordinates>35.3314,31.7051,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Khirbet Mazin</name><description>Status: Checked. building at the shore. Position: image, tile F018b (three-point transform with shift) (error approximately 50 m). Compared with the orthophoto of HA 136 (2024)</description><Point><coordinates>35.4429,31.6819,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Plateau Fort</name><description>Status: Checked. fort (Iron Age II). Position: image, tile A015c (25 Jun 1974) (error approximately 60 m). 50.5 by 49.5 m; no cistern recorded</description><Point><coordinates>35.6844,31.8416,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Habbasa</name><description>Status: Checked. fort with five cisterns. Position: image, tile A017e (1 Dec 1974) (error approximately 50 m). Row of roofless chambers, approximately 50 m; plan test with Prag and Barnes fig. 9</description><Point><coordinates>35.6793,31.8396,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Barakat</name><description>Status: Checked (form); Probable (position). fort. Position: image, tile A015c (error approximately 80 m). Grid reference in Prag and Barnes is 340 to 385 m south of this place (probable error in the paper)</description><Point><coordinates>35.6733,31.8527,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Kafrein dam, centre of the crest</name><description>Status: Checked. dam (1967). Position: elevation model (error approximately 30 m). Control point; crest 469 m on the image, 480 m published</description><Point><coordinates>35.6761,31.8511,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Tell Kafrein</name><description>Status: Checked. tell. Position: elevation model; OpenBible point 30 m (error approximately 30 m). Control point</description><Point><coordinates>35.6526,31.8507,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Tell el-Hammam, upper tell</name><description>Status: Checked. tell. Position: elevation model (middle of the ridge) (error approximately 50 m). Control point; OpenStreetMap outline agrees</description><Point><coordinates>35.674,31.8407,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Tree group at the foot of Tell el-Hammam</name><description>Status: Seen. probable springs. Position: image, tile A015c (error approximately 80 m). Probable place of the warm springs</description><Point><coordinates>35.6719,31.8387,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Umm Ḥadhar hill, dark patch</name><description>Status: Probable (hill). building with well-cistern (literature). Position: image, tile A015c (error approximately 100 m). Building not identified on the full-size window of 1 Dec 1974; two dark angular marks of 10 to 12 m with pits round them (modern by form)</description><Point><coordinates>35.6754,31.863,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Tell er-Rameh</name><description>Status: Checked. tell. Position: elevation model = published point; image 45 to 95 m (error approximately 30 m). The round mound beside the straight road</description><Point><coordinates>35.6443,31.8257,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Oval mound north-east of Tell er-Rameh</name><description>Status: Seen. hill. Position: image, tile A015c (error approximately 80 m). Not Tell er-Rameh; no name</description><Point><coordinates>35.6491,31.8299,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Tell Iktanu</name><description>Status: Checked (position); fort on the top Possible. tell. Position: elevation model; OpenBible point 60 m (error approximately 40 m). Long hill (approximately 400 m, north-east to south-west) north-west of the highway, with one rectangular outline of approximately 45 by 30 m on its top (image of 1 Dec 1974)</description><Point><coordinates>35.6713,31.8192,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Dark oval hill south of the highway</name><description>Status: Possible. hill. Position: image, tile A015c (error approximately 80 m). Possible second part of Iktanu; not confirmed</description><Point><coordinates>35.6745,31.8184,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Road works beside the Dead Sea road</name><description>Status: Seen. military works (20th century). Position: image, tile A015c (error approximately 80 m). Not ancient</description><Point><coordinates>35.6762,31.8217,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Machaerus, citadel hill</name><description>Status: Checked. fort with cisterns. Position: elevation model summit (image position is 213 m west: relief displacement) (error approximately 30 m). Identified on the image of 1974 before the excavations of 1978 to 1981</description><Point><coordinates>35.6238,31.5675,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Tell es-Samarat</name><description>Status: Possible (1974); Checked on the frames of 1918. tell. Position: direction and distance from Tell es-Sultan (Survey sheet): 210 degrees, 740 m (error approximately 80 m). Oval area of approximately 60 by 140 m in the fields in 1974</description><Point><coordinates>35.4404,31.8652,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Sugar mill (Tawahin es-Sukkar)</name><description>Status: Possible (1974); Checked on the frames of 1918. mill compound. Position: direction and distance from Tell es-Sultan (Survey sheet): 285 degrees, 535 m (error approximately 80 m). Buildings with trees in 1974; old compound not separated from farm buildings</description><Point><coordinates>35.4388,31.8723,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>ʿAin ez-Zara oasis (Callirrhoe)</name><description>Status: Probable. oasis with excavated buildings (literature). Position: image, tile F018b east shore window (centre of the field area) (error approximately 150 m). Farmed plain with spring courses and no shore road in 1974; the excavated buildings are not identified on the image</description><Point><coordinates>35.5637,31.5968,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Canyon mouth with a round fan north of the oasis</name><description>Status: Probable. wadi mouth. Position: image, tile F018b east shore window (error approximately 150 m). Probable mouth of Wadi Zarqa Maʿin</description><Point><coordinates>35.5655,31.62,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Document></kml>